@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.2.4
@changelog
  - Codename: 1.21 Gigawatts!
  - New: dynamic soft-key banks — a Sub-Bank computes its 8 keys live from the focused track (FX 1-8/9-16, Parameter Groups, or Track Colours); FX/Sends banks page by a chosen control
  - New: FX bank lights only the focused FX bright — press to focus, press again to solo + focus; Parameter Groups + Track Colours apply to all selected tracks (group on/off + names saved per project)
  - New: DynaMount mode — control up to 8 robotic mic stands from the UF8 strips (fader = X left/right, FLIP = Y distance, V-Pot = rotation, per-mount Home calibration + a Settings tab for name/IP/colour)
  - New: Keyboard macro binding type — capture a key chord live (or type it) and chain several with per-step delays; fires inside REAPER, Ctrl and Cmd kept distinct on macOS
  - Fix: umlauts (ä ö ü ß) render correctly on the UC1 and UF8 LCDs across track / marker / FX / preset names
  - New: UC1 channel-strip carousel shows the neighbouring track names for ~1 s after a switch, then collapses to the current name; the edited parameter stays on screen
  - New: favourites keep the plug-in's own non-mapped parameters (e.g. Analog Molecule "3D Flux" / "Thermal Bloom") across cycling — Channel-Strip and Bus-Compressor, saved with the project
